# Tenant-scoped data

Every read, write, query, upload, and AI context that touches persisted data MUST be scoped to the current tenant. Never load or mutate another tenant's data by id alone.

## Server

- Take `tenantId` from the authenticated user (`req.user.tenantId`), not from the request body/query (except trusted admin/setup flows).
- Include `tenantId` in every Mongo query filter and in every create payload.
- Services that accept an id must also accept `tenantId` and use both: `{ _id, tenantId }`.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — cross-tenant leak by id
const app = await Application.findById(applicationId);

// ✅ GOOD
const app = await Application.findOne({ _id: applicationId, tenantId });
```

## Client / API

- Do not send or trust a client-supplied `tenantId` for authorization.
- Tenant is implied by the session/JWT; UI only works with the current user's data.

## Checklist before shipping data work

- [ ] All finds/updates/deletes filter on `tenantId`
- [ ] New documents set `tenantId`
- [ ] File/storage keys and AI prompts that embed user data are tenant-bound
